  "body": "### Ordered list types are case-sensitive\r\n\r\nIt would make sense if instead of using type=\"A\" or type=\"a\", you used type=\"upper-alpha\" or type=\"lower-alpha\" because some backend implementations don't allow for case-sensitive attribute values. For the most part, HTML is not case-sensitive, so why would this area differ from that? And why aren't nested numbered lists showing the parent number? Looking at the spec's own table of contents shows this as lacking. ",
